<article class="env-lemma" id="0FGM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FGM">Lemma <span data-tag="0FGM">45.5.2</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a base field. The functor $\mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits ^ i(-)$ on the category of motives $M_ k$ is representable by $\mathbf{1}(-i)$, i.e., we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits ^ i(M) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{M_ k}(\mathbf{1}(-i), M)  \]
</div>
  <p> functorially in $M$ in $M_ k$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from the definitions and Lemma <a href="/tag/0FG0" data-tag="0FG0">45.3.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>